{"tool_name":"pyxit-segmentation-model-builder","contents":["neubias"],"fetched_metadata":{"neubias":{"body":[{"format":"basic_html","processed":"<p>This is a learnable segmentation algorithm based on ground-truth images and segmentation mask. It learns a multiple output pixel classification algorithm. It downloads from Cytomine-Core annotation images+alphamasks from project(s), build a segmentation (pixel classifier) model which is saved locally. Typical application: tumor detection in tissues in histology slides. It is based on \"Fast Multi-Class Image Annotation with Random Subwindows and Multiple Output Randomized Trees\" <a href=\"http://orbi.ulg.ac.be/handle/2268/12205\">http://orbi.ulg.ac.be/handle/2268/12205</a> and was used in \"A hybrid human-computer approach for large-scale image-based measurements using web services and machine learning\" <a href=\"http://orbi.ulg.ac.be/handle/2268/162084?locale=en\">http://orbi.ulg.ac.be/handle/2268/162084?locale=en</a></p>","summary":"","value":"<p>This is a learnable segmentation algorithm based on ground-truth images and segmentation mask. It learns a multiple output pixel classification algorithm. It downloads from Cytomine-Core annotation images+alphamasks from project(s), build a segmentation (pixel classifier) model which is saved locally. Typical application: tumor detection in tissues in histology slides. It is based on \"Fast Multi-Class Image Annotation with Random Subwindows and Multiple Output Randomized Trees\" http://orbi.ulg.ac.be/handle/2268/12205 and was used in \"A hybrid human-computer approach for large-scale image-based measurements using web services and machine learning\" http://orbi.ulg.ac.be/handle/2268/162084?locale=en</p>\r\n"}],"changed":[{"format":"Y-m-d\\TH:i:sP","value":"2019-10-18T16:52:00+00:00"}],"created":[{"format":"Y-m-d\\TH:i:sP","value":"2017-02-13T12:19:22+00:00"}],"default_langcode":[{"value":true}],"attribution_instructions":[],"comments_2023":[],"free_tagging":[],"give_feedba